# Tracked docs — commit and push together

The three live tracked docs are `docs/NOW.md`, `docs/ME.md`, and `docs/BUSINESS.md`.

`docs/archive/OLD_PLAN.md` is a **reference-only** archive (archived from the old
`docs/ATO_PLAN_v2.md`), not a live-status doc — it is **excluded** from this sync rule
and does not need to be cross-synced or pushed immediately when it changes.

When you update **any** of the three live docs:

1. Check the other two for overlapping facts (bundle ID, Stage 8 status, Apple/EAS, account type, what's next). Sync them in the **same** change — do not update only NOW.md.
2. Commit those doc updates together (with related code if this is the same unit of work).
3. **`git push` to origin immediately.** Never leave a commit that touches these docs sitting local-only.

This standing instruction overrides the default "don't push unless asked" rule for these three files only.
